227:{character:Reina Nanami} Seems you have really underestimated us, {var:player_nickname}! Éternité has secret recipes for everything, including our ice water! It's just that not many people order it, so I haven't had the chance to tell you.
228:{character:player} Oh, I'm sorry. I should have warned you I was going to come by. Is it a bad time?
229:{character:Saturne} No, not at all. It's actually a surprise! Please, come in, my friend.
230:{character:player} Oh, were you just playing Mahjong?
231:{character:Saturne} Ahaha! I wouldn't quite say that. I've heard that there's a game that's currently quite popular in One Han City, "Which tile to discard", so I wanted to try it out.
232:Saturne motions me to sit opposite him. Taking my seat, I notice a Mahjong hand in front of me: 1-Man, 2-Man, 3-Man, 3-Man, 4-Man, 5-Man, 7-Man, 8-Man, 9-Man, 4-Sou, 7-Pin. And the Pair is double 3-Pin. The 9 discarded tiles indicate that it's already the ninth turn.
233:{character:Saturne} The most fascinating thing about Mahjong is how different people play the same hand.
234:{character:Saturne} I'm curious how you'd play this, ignoring Round Wind, current points and all that.
