236:Saturne
237:{character:player} I'd Riichi with the 7-Pin.
238:{character:Saturne} Can you explain your thinking?
239:{character:player} Well, looking at the current discards and my hand, I'm in Tenpai waiting for one of five tiles and I've got a good pattern here. Moreover, all the 1-Pin are gone, but not a single 2-Pin has appeared. So maybe they're all still in the wall. If that's the case, I could get 2 Ura Dora if I'm lucky.
240:{character:Saturne} Haha, so it's like that! I used to think that doing business was a tactical and thrilling battle of wits, but Riichi Mahjong is no less exciting.
241:{character:player} That it is. If you hadn't said to ignore the points and all that, I think there could have a lot more options too.
242:{character:Saturne} It's just as I thought! You're talented at this sort of Mahjong. Have you ever considered... Entering a tournament?
243:{character:player} A tournament?
244:{character:Saturne} I presume you're calling upon me today because you have some answers to what we discussed before.
245:{character:Saturne} How interesting... Even the organizers don't remember the rules.
246:{character:Saturne} As happens, the tournament I just mentioned is precisely this one.
247:{character:player} How come you know things that even the Mahjong Soul Shrine priestess doesn't?
248:{character:Saturne} Haha! We businessmen have our own sources. But I suppose it can't hurt to tell you that One Han City has many information brokers. They loiter in the back alleys of the marketplaces, but provide reliable information... If you can afford it.
249:{character:player} Well, how do THEY know so much about the tournament?
250:{character:Saturne} Because one of the Four Greats recently got word that the Mahjong Soul Shrine tournament will soon be held once more.
251:{character:player} Really?! When?!!
252:{character:Saturne} That is up to her highness, the priestess of the Mahjong Soul Shrine. After all, is she not the true representative of the shrine's master?
253:{character:Saturne} However, it's hard to imagine such an innocent girl taking on such a heavy burden.
254:{character:player} I'd like to think she can. Despite her appearance, Ichihime has consistently done well as the Mahjong Soul Shrine priestess.
255:{character:Saturne} Well... I trust you, and if you vouch for her, then I'll trust her as well.
256:{character:player} Are you thinking of taking part in the tournament, Saturne?
257:{character:Saturne} Is that an invitation to play with you?
258:{character:player} Hmm, I suppose it is. I don't think many people would refuse the chance to take part in a tournament with a friend.
259:{character:Saturne} Well, I must not let my friend down! Haha, today's shaping up to be a good day—not only have we cleared up some of the mystery surrounding the legend, but we've got an appointment in the diary too.
260:{character:Saturne} I do believe this calls for a celebration.
261:{character:player} I'd play the 7-Pin and go for Hidden Tenpai.
262:{character:player} Currently, the player opposite has discarded 4/5/6 tiles in three consecutive turns, while having made 1 call. Maybe they have already achieved Tenpai, so right now Riichi is risky. What's more, if I can hold out for the 6-Man, that has the potential to improve my hand.
263:{character:Saturne} Ah, so that's why...
264:{character:player} Huh?
265:{character:Saturne} Sorry, I suddenly thought of a friend and got a little distracted.
266:{character:player} Did the other person also do this "Which tile to discard"?
267:{character:Saturne} To be honest, he left just before you arrived.
268:{character:Saturne} He was sitting where you are now, facing the same problem of "Which tile to discard", and actually made the same choice as you. However, this particular friend is a taciturn type, and wouldn't tell me his reasoning no matter how many times I asked. In fact, he even asked me...
269:{character:Saturne} "Why don't you go for Hidden Tenpai?"
270:{character:Saturne} That's it. I can't really do a good impression of him, haha.
271:{character:player} I thought it was quite good! Reminded me of one of my friends, actually.
272:{character:Saturne} Oh?
273:{character:player} This friend of mine loves his Hidden Tenpai. He likes to say "Hidden Tenpai is the safest way to play, lurking near the target, waiting for the right moment to strike."
274:{character:Saturne} Haha! This friend of yours sounds like an interesting character.
275:{character:player} That reminds me! Is your recent guest the same friend you've been waiting for these past few days?
276:{character:Saturne} Precisely so! His work keeps him phenomenally busy, so he could only make it today... Although he only stayed a short while before scurrying off again.
277:{character:player} That's a shame. It's rare to meet someone who thinks the same. How great would it be if we could play a round or two together!
278:{character:Saturne} We might as well! This friend of mine should be in One Han City for a while longer, though he seems to have his eye on someone, so it might be a little hard to get him on board! But I'm sure we'll find a time to play.
279:{character:Saturne} Anyway, I presume you're paying me a visit today because you have some answers to what we discussed before, no?
280:{character:Saturne} I never had any impression of the Four Great Jyanshis, but now that you name them, I realize that they're all pretty important people in One Han City... It's just that they don't often broadcast their status as the Four Greats, so it was hard to connect the dots.
281:{character:player} That's right! Before I knew Kazuha Saionji, I never would have thought that such a young, beautiful woman would be one of the Four Greats. But, after thinking about it, I don't see why not, as if...
282:{character:Saturne} As if she was born to be one of the Four Greats!
283:{character:player} Yeah, that's right.
284:{character:Saturne} Haha! Well, seeing as we have some clues now, I trust we'll be getting to the bottom of this legend in no time at all.
285:{character:Saturne} I think some celebration drinks are in order!
